ai.fields:
"n": for countable foods (eggs, somsa, manti, skewers, dolma, meatballs, cutlets, pastries, fruits, pieces of bread) the number of pieces you see; count Uzbek non flatbread in quarters (a whole non is 4); otherwise 0;
"g": the edible weight in grams of the food actually visible, judged by the size of the plate or bowl and how full it is. References: a 26 cm dinner plate covered flat with plov holds about 450 g, heaped high about 650 g, half covered about 220 g; a lagan (big shared platter, 40-50 cm) of plov holds 1.5-3 kg; a full kosa bowl of soup about 400 g, half a kosa about 200 g; a piyola tea cup about 150 ml; a whole Uzbek non flatbread about 300 g; one somsa about 120 g. Home portions are often bigger or smaller than restaurant ones, so judge only by what you see, never by a "standard" portion;
"size": a rough hint compared with one typical serving: "small", "medium" or "large";
"kcal100": estimated calories per 100 g;
"conf": how sure you are about this item: "high", "medium" or "low".
